he birth-day celebrations of arjuna. (Ādi Parva, Chapter 129, Verse 63).\n(v) In temples his idols are installed with sword in hand and seated on an ass. (agni purāṇa, Chapter 51).", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["nirRRiti", "nirRRiti_1", "nirRiti", "nirRiti_1", "nirRti", "nirRti_1", "nirRuti", "nirRuti_1", "nirṛti", "nirṛti_1", "निरृति", "నిరృతి", "నిరృతి_౧", "ನಿರೃತಿ", "ನಿರೃತಿ_೧"], "synonyms_slp1": ["nirRRiti", "nirRRiti_1", "nirRiti", "nirRiti_1", "nirRti", "nirRti_1", "nirRuti", "nirRuti_1", "nirṛti", "nirṛti_1", "nirfti", "నిరృతి", "నిరృతి_౧", "ನಿರೃತಿ", "ನಿರೃತಿ_೧"]}], "nirfti_२": [{"id": "nirfti_२", "headword": "निरृति_२", "headword_slp1": "nirfti_२", "fold": "nirfti_२", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "purana-encyclopedia", "senses": [{"gloss": "निरृति २\n\nNIRṚTI II . Wife of the deva called adharma. She had three sons called bhaya, mahābhaya and antaka. These Rākṣasas are known as Nairṛtas. (Ādi Parva, Chapter 66, Verse 54).", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["nirRRiti", "nirRRiti_2", "nirRiti", "nirRiti_2", "nirRti", "nirRti_2", "nirRuti", "nirRuti_2", "nirṛti", "nirṛti_2", "निरृति", "నిరృతి", "నిరృతి_౨", "ನಿರೃತಿ", "ನಿರೃತಿ_೨"], "synonyms_slp1": ["nirRRiti", "nirRRiti_2", "nirRiti", "nirRiti_2", "nirRti", "nirRti_2", "nirRuti", "nirRuti_2", "nirṛti", "nirṛti_2", "nirfti", "నిరృతి", "నిరృతి_౨", "ನಿರೃತಿ", "ನಿರೃತಿ_೨"]}]}